WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
Two supermarket trolleys
stand side by side.

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.850
One is empty.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.990
The other is piled high
with a week's shopping.

4
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.110
You give each one
exactly the same push.

5
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.870
The empty trolley shoots
off down the aisle.

6
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.710
The full one barely creeps forward.

7
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.250
Same push, same trolley design,
completely different result.

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.470
Why does the same force make
them move so differently?

9
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.530
In this mission, you'll find
out what happens when the forces

10
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.190
on an object are balanced.

11
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.590
You'll combine forces into
a single resultant force,

12
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.870
and see what that resultant
force does to an object's motion.

13
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: explain why the
same push gives such different

14
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.860
results.
